h4. Motivation
fh-sync works with object hashes to compare if object was changed. 
Hashing has 3 major disadvantages:
- users needs to be aware of hashing method and reject autogenerated fields.
- It's performance intensive
- requires object to be ordered (Sorting operation)
Most of the sync libraries allow developer to supply compare method that is used to determine that object was changed. For example when using mongoose developers may relay on last_updated field or use _.isMatch(clientObj,dbObj). Hashing seems to be really good default behavior, but it will be better to allow developers to supply custom methods to determine if object was changed. Developers now are forced to hack sync framework to achieve this with some common mistakes and unexpected results like collisions.
Compare methods are common in many different languages and frameworks. For example in java equals method is used to add element to hash map and by default hash is used.
h4. Example API
{code}
function hasChanged( clientObj, serverObj){
 return clientObject.updatedAt!==serverObj.updatedAt;
}
syncDataset.setComparator(hasChanged);
{code}
h4. Alternative
Alternative for this will to be still use hashing method, but allow developers to specify what fields should be taken into account when performing hashing. 
This aproach is used in the most popular sync databases. For example see: 
